            <ArticleTitle>6-exo-trig Michael addition-lactonizations for catalytic enantioselective chromenone synthesis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2555-2558</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c6cc10178j</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The catalytic enantioselective 6-exo-trig Michael addition-lactonization of enone-acid substrates to form cis-chromenones with high diastereo- and enantiocontrol was developed using the commercially available isothiourea tetramisole. An acidic workup proved necessary to minimize product epimerization and maximize product er, providing cis-chromenones in excellent yield, and with excellent diastereo- and enantioselectivity.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
